Texels drawn past the screen's sides are decoded too (warecomp STATUS.md
round 11).

RDP::drawRect records which texels a rect samples, cut to the scissor, and
the texture cache decodes only those. With the game's full-screen scissor
(0-320) that stopped at the old right edge, while the draw itself goes on
past it in an expanded aspect ratio (0025): beyond the last decoded texel
the sampler mirrored, so Worms Armageddon's landscape showed mirrored about
x = 320 on the right of a widescreen window. A scissor spanning the whole
colour image, without origins, now doesn't cut the sampled range
horizontally, the same way 0025 treats it for drawing.

--- a/src/hle/rt64_rdp.cpp
+++ b/src/hle/rt64_rdp.cpp
@@ -1291,9 +1291,21 @@
 
         // Update the tracked texcoords for the used tiles. Use scissor intersection to figure out 
         // what the bounds of the real sampling will be if necessary.
-        const bool computeIntersection = !scissorRect.isNull() && !scissorRect.fullyInside(drawRect);
+        //
+        // A scissor spanning the whole colour image (without origins) is just the screen, and with an
+        // expanded aspect ratio it doesn't cut the draw horizontally (the framebuffer renderer widens
+        // it): the texels past the screen's sides are sampled too, so they must be decoded as well.
+        FixedRect samplingScissor = scissorRect;
+        const bool screenScissor = !scissorRect.isNull() && (scissorRect.ulx <= 0) && (scissorRect.lrx >= (int32_t(colorImage.width) << 2)) &&
+            (extended.scissorLeftOriginStack[scissorStackSize - 1] == G_EX_ORIGIN_NONE) && (extended.scissorRightOriginStack[scissorStackSize - 1] == G_EX_ORIGIN_NONE);
+        if (screenScissor) {
+            samplingScissor.ulx = std::min(samplingScissor.ulx, drawRect.ulx);
+            samplingScissor.lrx = std::max(samplingScissor.lrx, drawRect.lrx);
+        }
+
+        const bool computeIntersection = !samplingScissor.isNull() && !samplingScissor.fullyInside(drawRect);
         if (computeIntersection) {
-            const FixedRect intersectionRect = scissorRect.intersection(drawRect);
+            const FixedRect intersectionRect = samplingScissor.intersection(drawRect);
             if (!intersectionRect.isNull()) {
                 const int32_t leftPixels = intersectionRect.left(true) - drawRect.left(true);
                 const int32_t topPixels = intersectionRect.top(true) - drawRect.top(true);
